  "details": "Replace avatar diamonds with Avatar Impostor when using features such as safety settings, distance based hiding, and avatar limit hiding.\n\nThis will allow users to “see” other people’s avatars instead of player diamonds, assisting in making populated instances seem.. well.. populated, as opposed to only seeing a handful of avatars and a sea of diamonds.\n\nThe most useful scenarios are for distance-based hiding, as it will be practically unnoticeable due to the distances at which the impostor is likely to be seen from, and for safety settings, as it will be more clear which avatars you are showing before you choose to do so. Also, since Impostors have started Auto-Generating, it should be convenient and accurate for most avatars.\n\nThis should be an ***optional feature*** that can be enabled on the client through the menu, functioning similar to how Impostors work in games like SecondLife, mostly due to Impostors consuming a non-zero amount of resources (albeit far less than Very Poor avatars), so users should be able to toggle the setting as they see fit",
